# Windows Computer Use reports the wrong focused element; Calculator index operations vary across window lifecycles

Submitted with user authorization on 2026-10-31. No private transcripts, credentials, images, user documents, machine usernames or local installation paths are included.

## Environment

- Official Windows desktop package: OpenAI.Codex 26.1027.3384.0.
- Windows DisplayVersion 26H2, build 26300.9711.
- Sky runtime identifier: cua_node/5c41f77a7900391c; package 0.7.13.
- Signed native SHA-256: 49c7f43da0c2a9dbcadfb0c993058147018bf7c1d0fde4360de11ace2c98f45d. Signature valid.
- Vendor native and computer_use_client_base.js unchanged. Local JS changes restore two genuine Store catalogue target paths/launch aliases and add a content-free observer around the existing transport. The native-pipe vendor body, original parameters, framing, result/error identity and approval flow are preserved and tested. This is disclosed rather than presented as a pristine-JS installation.

## Stable focus reproduction

A standard WPF window has two TextBoxes, Alpha then Beta. On Loaded, it focuses Beta directly. Standard TextBoxAutomationPeer wrappers only record their own values and forward the original ValuePattern.

1. Launch the existing fixture via the supported sky.launch_app API; select its unique returned window and activate it.
2. Capture accessibility text. The application records Alpha.HasKeyboardFocus=False and Beta.HasKeyboardFocus=True. Its first focus event is Beta.GotFocus; no Alpha.GotFocus occurs.
3. The first and later get_window_state results nevertheless identify Alpha as focused_element. document_text comes from Beta.
4. After a fresh observation, perform one set_value on the returned Beta index. The provider confirms Beta received and completed the operation; tree value and document_text update to the new Beta value. focused_element still identifies Alpha.

Expected: focused_element reflects the actual focused Beta control, or is omitted when focus cannot be reliably determined.

The fixture is outside the two-application compatibility scope. Its previously accepted binary was reused without recompilation. Physical Escape, approvals and original input dispatch are preserved.

## Calculator index evidence and positive controls

Store Calculator 11.2607.0.0 initially exposed a complete tree, but separate single indexed clicks returned index-not-cached for Seven, Eight and Nine. A text-only Five operation returned geometry unavailable. A screenshot-backed Six operation returned success, followed by a missing original window; the intended numeral was not verified, so it is not classified as a successful hit or a proven close-button mis-target.

Later indexed Three, Four, Two and Nine operations succeeded with visible and accessibility-confirmed results. These include temporary path-hook disable/restore, a fresh native connection, and EXE-path launch. Therefore neither the local hook, startup route nor connection temperature is established as the sole cause. No input was replayed after an uncertain outcome.

Observation-to-action intervals were measured rather than called immediate: initial cases 18.644–46.213 seconds, and one later cold-connection success 62.391 seconds. There is no demonstrated universal short expiry threshold.

## Diagnostic request

Observed ordinary native state responses expose only global accessibilityRevision, accessibilitySnapshotCount and captureCachedSessionCount. Please provide supported diagnostics or a signed diagnostic build correlating:

- published snapshot and action lookup: canonical app/cache key, process ID, root/input HWND, per-window snapshot revision, element-map count and requested-ID membership;
- resolved element bounds, screenshot generation and final coordinate space;
- UIA cached focus BOOL / CompareElements result through focus aggregation to focused_element formatting.

Hash-locked static inspection locates the exact index-not-cached branch after application-cache selection and a full 64-bit ID lookup in a HashMap; it is not a dense-array subscript. CachedHasKeyboardFocus and its fallback check both test the returned BOOL, so an HRESULT-only explanation is not established. The precise cause remains unproven.

83 local regression tests pass, covering original request framing, one-dispatch semantics, result/error identity, stop/approval behavior and observer privacy. These tests do not claim the native issues are fixed. Local trace collection is disabled after the investigation. Full private session logs are not attached.

## Reproduction source: the INITIAL_BETA path

The small source listing below resolves the fixture's INITIAL_BETA compile-time branch: Alpha appears before Beta, and Loaded directly focuses Beta. Unused build branches are removed. The standard TextBoxAutomationPeer supplies TextPattern unchanged; only this fixture's own property reads and forwarded ValuePattern calls are logged.

This is a source export for maintainers. No new executable was built or run during this export, and no binary/source reproducibility claim is made for a new build. The historically tested accepted executable's SHA-256 is `60752a79a8d7a44bda74e6d1be9745c60e512241949fe16f06ee834847b4f365`; the reviewed current source before branch resolution is `8f2d8a11d6abb69a4c44de1bab09ce3765d0e97fbb6a81a39848c51f905c161f`. The earlier live failures and independent selection-range evidence remain as documented.

Save these three files together in a fresh disposable directory on a Windows development machine with .NET Framework WPF references. The build script compiles only this resolved initial-Beta source; it does not launch it. Use the documented Computer Use window2 API for the subsequent fixture run: select its unique actual returned Window, observe both screenshot and accessibility text, compare focused_element with Beta's visible caret and the fixture's Loaded/HasFocus records, then close its own window normally. Keep observation and input in separate calls and do not replay uncertain input.

Expected: focused_element identifies the actually focused Beta control. The failure already reported on the signed native build identifies Alpha instead. A further Tab-to-button control must identify the button rather than either editor. The local log file belongs only to this disposable fixture; no actual log, screenshot, private data or executable is uploaded here.

<details>
<summary>FreshnessProbe.cs — resolved initial-Beta source</summary>

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Diagnostics;
using System.Globalization;
using System.IO;
using System.Text;
using System.Windows;
using System.Windows.Automation;
using System.Windows.Automation.Peers;
using System.Windows.Automation.Provider;
using System.Windows.Controls;

// Passive standard WPF provider instrumentation, limited to this window.
// No external UIA client, native helper protocol, input injection, or network.
static class FreshLog
{
    static readonly object gate = new object();
    static readonly Dictionary<string, long> last = new Dictionary<string, long>();
    public static readonly string FileName = Path.Combine(AppDomain.CurrentDomain.BaseDirectory,
        "freshness-probe-" + DateTime.Now.ToString("yyyyMMdd-HHmmss-fff") + ".tsv");
    public static void Write(string id, string kind, string detail, bool critical = false)
    {
        lock (gate)
        {
            long tick = Stopwatch.GetTimestamp();
            string key = id + "|" + kind + "|" + detail;
            long previous;
            if (!critical && last.TryGetValue(key, out previous) && tick - previous < Stopwatch.Frequency * 2) return;
            last[key] = tick;
            File.AppendAllText(FileName, DateTimeOffset.Now.ToString("o") + "\t" + id + "\t" + kind + "\t" +
                detail.Replace('\t', ' ').Replace('\r', ' ').Replace('\n', ' ') + "\r\n", new UTF8Encoding(false));
        }
    }
}

class FreshEdit : TextBox
{
    public readonly string ProbeId;
    public FreshEdit(string id, string name)
    {
        ProbeId = id;
        AutomationProperties.SetAutomationId(this, id);
        AutomationProperties.SetName(this, name);
        Text = id + "-epoch-0";
        Height = 42;
        Margin = new Thickness(0, 4, 0, 24);
        GotKeyboardFocus += (s,e) => FreshLog.Write(ProbeId, "GotFocus", "true", true);
        LostKeyboardFocus += (s,e) => FreshLog.Write(ProbeId, "LostFocus", "false", true);
    }
    protected override AutomationPeer OnCreateAutomationPeer() { return new FreshPeer(this); }
}

class FreshPeer : TextBoxAutomationPeer
{
    readonly FreshEdit edit;
    IValueProvider wrapper;
    public FreshPeer(FreshEdit owner) : base(owner) { edit = owner; }
    public override object GetPattern(PatternInterface pattern)
    {
        object value = base.GetPattern(pattern);
        if (pattern == PatternInterface.Value && value is IValueProvider)
        {
            if (wrapper == null) wrapper = new LoggedValue(edit, (IValueProvider)value);
            return wrapper;
        }
        return value;
    }
    protected override string GetNameCore()
    {
        string value = base.GetNameCore();
        FreshLog.Write(edit.ProbeId, "Name", value);
        return value;
    }
    protected override bool HasKeyboardFocusCore()
    {
        bool value = base.HasKeyboardFocusCore();
        FreshLog.Write(edit.ProbeId, "HasFocus", value.ToString());
        return value;
    }
    protected override Rect GetBoundingRectangleCore()
    {
        Rect value = base.GetBoundingRectangleCore();
        FreshLog.Write(edit.ProbeId, "Bounds", value.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture));
        return value;
    }
    class LoggedValue : IValueProvider
    {
        readonly FreshEdit edit;
        readonly IValueProvider original;
        public LoggedValue(FreshEdit owner, IValueProvider provider) { edit = owner; original = provider; }
        public bool IsReadOnly { get { bool v = original.IsReadOnly; FreshLog.Write(edit.ProbeId, "IsReadOnly", v.ToString()); return v; } }
        public string Value { get { string v = original.Value; FreshLog.Write(edit.ProbeId, "Value", v); return v; } }
        public void SetValue(string value)
        {
            FreshLog.Write(edit.ProbeId, "SetValue.begin", value, true);
            try { original.SetValue(value); FreshLog.Write(edit.ProbeId, "SetValue.return", "success", true); }
            catch (Exception e) { FreshLog.Write(edit.ProbeId, "SetValue.throw", e.GetType().Name, true); throw; }
        }
    }
}

class FreshnessProbe : Window
{
    readonly FreshEdit alpha = new FreshEdit("FreshAlpha", "Fresh Alpha epoch 0");
    readonly FreshEdit beta = new FreshEdit("FreshBeta", "Fresh Beta epoch 0");
    readonly TextBlock status = new TextBlock();
    int epoch;
    public FreshnessProbe()
    {
        Title = "CU Freshness Probe";
        Title = "CU Freshness Probe Beta Initial";
        Width = 590; Height = 520; Top = 50;
        Left = Math.Max(24, SystemParameters.WorkArea.Right - Width - 24);
        FontSize = 16;
        var panel = new StackPanel { Margin = new Thickness(24) };
        panel.Children.Add(new TextBlock { Text = "Stable controls; changing Name, ReadOnly, bounds and focus.", TextWrapping = TextWrapping.Wrap });
        panel.Children.Add(new TextBlock { Text = Path.GetFileName(FreshLog.FileName), Margin = new Thickness(0,12,0,12) });
        panel.Children.Add(new TextBlock { Text = "Alpha" });
        panel.Children.Add(alpha);
        panel.Children.Add(new TextBlock { Text = "Beta" });
        panel.Children.Add(beta);
        var advance = new Button { Content = "Advance properties", Focusable = false, Height = 44, Margin = new Thickness(0,8,0,8) };
        advance.Click += (s,e) => Advance();
        panel.Children.Add(advance);
        var close = new Button { Content = "Close freshness probe", Height = 44 };
        close.Click += (s,e) => Close();
        panel.Children.Add(close);
        panel.Children.Add(status);
        Content = panel;
        Loaded += (s,e) => {
            beta.Focus();
            Record("Loaded");
        };
        Closed += (s,e) => FreshLog.Write("Window", "Closed", "true", true);
    }
    void Advance()
    {
        epoch++;
        alpha.IsReadOnly = epoch % 2 == 1;
        AutomationProperties.SetName(alpha, "Fresh Alpha epoch " + epoch);
        AutomationProperties.SetName(beta, "Fresh Beta epoch " + epoch);
        alpha.Text = "alpha-epoch-" + epoch;
        beta.Text = "beta-epoch-" + epoch;
        alpha.Margin = new Thickness(0, 4 + (epoch % 2) * 16, 0, 24 - (epoch % 2) * 16);
        if (epoch % 2 == 1) beta.Focus(); else alpha.Focus();
        UpdateLayout();
        status.Text = "Epoch " + epoch + "; Alpha read-only=" + alpha.IsReadOnly;
        Record("Advance");
    }
    void Record(string operation)
    {
        FreshLog.Write("Window", operation, "epoch=" + epoch + ";alphaFocus=" + alpha.IsKeyboardFocused +
            ";betaFocus=" + beta.IsKeyboardFocused + ";alphaReadOnly=" + alpha.IsReadOnly +
            ";alphaName=" + AutomationProperties.GetName(alpha) + ";alphaScreen=" + alpha.PointToScreen(new Point(0,0)), true);
    }
    [STAThread]
    static void Main() { new Application().Run(new FreshnessProbe()); }
}
```

</details>

