package version: 2026.10.9 (unmodified)
buildId: 2026.10.9-0ad0ce34e388-2026-11-01T23-46-08.284Z
tarball bytes: 111396419
tarball SHA256: 0e6ccd27669266fb695abb06f548572c13b245b73cb56ec605c69294da504049
```

The packed main-branch manifest fields match the final source manifest, including update preflight protocol 1 and state/agent schema versions 39. These fields are inherited from main; this PR adds no schema/protocol change. An explicit local artifact allows testing the new build at the unchanged package version; neither baseline nor candidate is relabeled.

The native survivor runs the genuinely installed published stable updater against the exact canonical tarball above. Its final host wrapper exits **0** after **1177.79 seconds**; the inner summary has `status: passed`, `updateOutcome: success` and no failure. All **47 phases / 94 start/finish events** pass, including:

- baseline CLI configuration recipe, package activation/identity and state/config checks;
- 8 volume conversations across 2 agents, 30 materialized volume events and 8 volume cron jobs, plus the canonical baseline fixtures;
- Gateway startup, health/readiness/status and all 8 conversation-history RPCs before and after a manual stop/start;
- Doctor idempotence in 119 seconds within the owner-computed 242-second budget.

The requested fixture settings are 8 sessions × 5 events and 8 cron jobs; special missing/metadata-only cases mean 30 materialized volume events. The whole-state idempotence inventory includes baseline fixtures (11 sessions, 33 events and 11 cron jobs), so these are bounded synthetic-volume assertions, not a claim about a production-sized installation.

The recorded native invocation uses the pinned proof harness described below, from the `0ad0ce34` source checkout:

```sh
