Closes #141806

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: memory_search and memory_get invoke bundled memory-core instead of the selected memory plugin when memory-core remains enabled as a dreaming sidecar.

## User Impact

User impact: custom memory plugins receive their recall calls while memory-core can continue providing its standing-intent and dreaming sidecar services. No configuration migration is required.

Visible change: when another memory plugin owns the slot (for example Knowledge or `memory-lancedb`) and Memory Core stays loaded only as the dreaming sidecar, agents no longer get Memory Core's `memory_search`/`memory_get` over workspace memory files. Recall comes from the selected plugin's own tools. Active Memory's default `memory_search`/`memory_get` fallback then records recall as unavailable (existing missing-tools path) unless the selected plugin declares `recallToolNames` or `toolsAllow` is configured, instead of silently answering from Memory Core's index.

## Why This Change Was Made

Use the existing selected-memory-slot check for recall tool registration as well as index startup. Keep the sidecar registration outside that check.

## Evidence

- Scenario: The selected memory plugin handles both standard recall tools; The unselected memory-core sidecar still serves intent list
- Entry: node CHECKOUT/openclaw.mjs gateway run --bind loopback --port PORT; public WebSocket sessions.create, plugins.list, tools.invoke(memory_get/memory_search/intent); disputed owner ran unmocked: extensions/memory-core/index.ts, through ordinary plugin discovery and tools.invoke
- Same command on base `b0fdadd` and head `d6bddcf`: `node proof-memory-slot.mjs CHECKOUT NEW_OUTPUT_DIR EXPECTED_VERSION`
